            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MiniWhisper 1.10.0</h2>

<h3>Fn key combinations can no longer be bound</h3>

<p>
    Shortcuts that combine <b>Fn with another key</b> — such as Fn+W — no longer
    work. macOS offers no way to register them without also swallowing the plain
    key everywhere, which would mean binding Fn+W stopped W from reaching any app
    at all.
</p>

<p>
    If you had one, an orange warning marker now appears next to it in the menu
    bar and in Settings. Click the shortcut and record a new one to fix it.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><b>Fn (Globe) on its own</b> is unaffected.</li>
    <li>
        Shortcuts using <b>arrow keys or function keys</b> are unaffected and
        carry over automatically.
    </li>
</ul>
]]></description>
